sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Request A (user 41)
  participant B as Request B (user 77)
  participant R as Redis single command thread
  Note over R: stock:sale-1 = 1

  A->>R: EVALSHA reserve.lua (user 41)
  B->>R: EVALSHA reserve.lua (user 77)
  Note over R: scripts are queued and run one at a time
  R->>R: A: GET stock = 1, not in buyers set -> DECR -> 0, SADD user 41, SET hold TTL 120s
  R-->>A: 1 (accepted)
  R->>R: B: GET stock = 0 -> return -1
  R-->>B: -1 (sold out)
  Note over A,B: exactly one unit sold, no lock held by the application
